# Add passkey sign-in
{.lead} Let people sign in with a passkey instead of a password, without breaking the existing email-and-password flow.

## Groundwork

Map the current auth path and stand up the WebAuthn pieces behind a flag before any user sees a change.

```mdp:tasks
- [x] Audit every caller of the current login endpoint
- [x] Pick a WebAuthn library and add it behind a feature flag
- [~] Model the `credential` table and its migration
- [ ] Add a server endpoint to start and finish registration
```

:::callout warning
The password flow must keep working untouched for everyone while passkeys roll out. Treat any change to the existing endpoint as out of scope here.
:::

---

## Implementation

Wire the client ceremony to the new endpoints and let an account hold more than one passkey.

```mdp:tasks
- [ ] Build the register-a-passkey screen in account settings
- [ ] Build the sign-in-with-a-passkey button on the login screen
- [ ] Support multiple passkeys per account, each with a label
- [ ] Fall back to password automatically when WebAuthn is unavailable
```

```mdp:flow
Create challenge -> Browser signs it -> Verify and store credential
```

---

## Verification & rollout

Prove it works across the common platforms, then open the flag a little at a time.

```mdp:tasks
- [ ] Add end-to-end tests for register, sign-in, and the password fallback
- [ ] Manually verify on iOS, Android, and a desktop browser
- [ ] Roll out to 5% of accounts, then 50%, then everyone
```

:::callout recommendation
Keep the flag on a kill switch through the full rollout. If sign-in success dips on any platform, flip it off and fall back to passwords with no deploy.
:::
